  ],
  "sharedModel": [
    "Align the left horizontal metric once. Translate both current and original simple-outline X points and original phantom coordinates into that frame. Preserve unscaled design coordinates and independently scaled absolute right originals.",
    "Current right metrics add an independently rounded advance to the aligned left coordinate. Do not round the absolute right coordinate as though it were a displacement.",
    "Composite children retain their completed alignment. A Windows parent program sees its own phantom metrics; USE_MY_METRICS still selects the completed child paint origin afterward. Preserve the distinct FreeType policy.",
    "One allocation-free initializer is shared by the simple and composite loaders. Borrowed points remain exclusive and bounded, shifted points observe cancellation, and existing reservations/cleanup own every array. Shaping, fitting, glyph sampling, preblend and alpha rounding remain unchanged."
  ],
